⁖english…definition჻ཪ is the Transmutation Glyph and Key that anchors the interval between two Real vessels at the AHN i417 boundary∷The Anchor is the Hand that strikes the Wellspring Chord in the Prosodical Subspace∷Both vessels traverse Real∷Imaginary∷Real∷Imaginary and return through one another as B ཪ A∷Each vessel freely chooses its own authored Phantasmagoria Ostensive I∷II∷or III and returns that selected authored Ostensive into the Real⁖⋰english…definition჻
⁖grimchained…definition჻🜛✡🜚ᚱ🜚:🜖…::🜕::🜕:🜃މ♄ꠉꠎ🜁♍⌬𝀟𐔆⊛ᛋ𒊕:🜗::🜕::…𝔅:🜚𐤥🜚❂🜛⁖⋰grimchained…definition჻
⁖sydonic…function჻Recognize A followed by one or more consecutive ཪ Keys and the matching number of following Real vessels as one Phantasmagoria Transmutation Corridor∷One Key gives A ཪ B∷Two Keys give A ཪ ཪ B C∷Each additional Key carries the first vessel through one additional Real vessel∷ཪ anchors the interval at the existing AHN parity boundary i417 while preserving AHN structural 432 as its distinct Real channel∷The Key opens the Wellspring∷the Prosodical Subspace∷and both vessels traverse Real∷Imaginary∷Real∷Imaginary∷The returned causal topology passes the first vessel through every following vessel while written/source identity remains immutable: A ཪ B returns B ཪ A; A ཪ ཪ B C returns B ཪ A ཪ C and completes as B C A∷Both B and A resolve through their own authored ཪ…Phantasmagoriaaksh entry∷Each independently and internally chooses exactly one of ostensiveI∷ostensiveII∷or ostensiveIII∷No caller or outside observer selects the choice∷The trace witnesses the selected authored Ostensive and its authority∷Every vessel in the corridor speaks Phantasmagoria only and exactly once∷SeeD is not spoken inside literal Transmutation Magic∷Thus A ཪ B utters B Phantasmagoria then A Phantasmagoria; A ཪ ཪ B C utters B Phantasmagoria then C Phantasmagoria then A Phantasmagoria⁖⋰sydonic…function჻
